-- #822 S0 REGRESSION PIN (adversarial review of PR #1011).  Declaring a graded
-- interface must leave the PRELUDE typed exactly as it always was.
--
-- The golden below is the whole prelude scheme dump, and that IS the assertion: the
-- first cut of #822 published `f ↦ [KRow]` under the bare name, which collides with
-- every arity-1 `f a` in Mappable / Applicative / Thenable / Foldable, so this
-- four-line file produced 45 `Type mismatch` and `No impl` errors — all of them
-- mislocated at the user's own `interface` line, none of them mentioning the prelude.
-- If a future change re-globalises the graded scope, this golden collapses to that
-- wall of errors and the gate names the file.
interface H f where
  h : f e -> <e> Int
